---
source: src/main.rs
expression: "render_help_snapshot(&[\"monitor\", \"create\"])"
---
Create an uptime monitor

Usage: hooklistener monitor create [OPTIONS] <NAME> <URL>

Arguments:
  <NAME>  Monitor display name
  <URL>   URL to check (http:// or https://)

Options:
      --method <METHOD>         HTTP method [default: GET] [possible values: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH,
                                DELETE, HEAD]
      --expected-status <CODE>  Expected HTTP status code [default: 200]
      --interval <INTERVAL>     Check interval [default: 5m] [possible values: 1m, 5m, 10m, 30m,
                                60m]
      --body-contains <TEXT>    Text the response body must contain
      --body <BODY>             Request body to send with POST, PUT, or PATCH
      --failure-threshold <N>   Consecutive failures before alerting [default: 2]
      --no-email                Disable email notifications for this monitor
  -o, --org <ORG_ID>            Organization ID (overrides the configured default)
  -h, --help                    Print help

Global options:
      --json               Output supported command responses or event streams as JSON
      --color <COLOR>      Styling policy for human output [default: auto] [possible values: auto,
                           always, never]
      --yes                Confirm destructive commands without an interactive prompt
      --log-level <LEVEL>  Log level [default: info] [possible values: trace, debug, info, warn,
                           error]
      --log-dir <DIR>      Directory for log files
      --log-stdout         Also write logs to stdout
